    "name": "os-lab-setup",
    "description": "Bootstraps an isolated lab repo for a skill improvement run: initializes git, copies the plugin as real files, renders eval-instructions.md, commits the baseline and offers manual or autonomous launch options. Trigger with \"set up an eval lab\", \"bootstrap the eval repo\", \"prepare the test repo for skill evaluation\", \"create an eval environment for this skill\", \"set up the lab space for this skill\", or when starting a new skill optimization run that needs a standalone test environment. DO NOT USE to run the improvement loop (use os-lab-loop), to score a change (use os-lab-scorer), to plan what to improve (use os-lab-planner), or to backport lab results to master (use os-lab-backport).\n",
